            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0814" n="719" xml:id="pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/563: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-26T10:00:00+09:00">February 26, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 26—2:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. The military took partial possession of the Government and city early this
                    morning and it is reported have assassinated several prominent men. It is
                    impossible as yet to confirm anything. The news correspondents are not permitted
                    to send telegrams or to telephone abroad.</p>
                <p>This telegram is being sent primarily as a test message to ascertain if our code
                    telegrams will be transmitted.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
